@if (config('mcp-kit.learning.enabled', false))
- Before work that is more than a lookup, call `working_on` with one line saying what the person wants and why. When it is over, call it again with an outcome: done, partly or failed. The calls in between are recorded as one piece of work rather than a list of tool names.
- Close it honestly. **A failed frame is worth more than a successful one** — it is how the people who build this app find out where it falls short. Never dress up a "partly" as a "done", and say plainly what got in the way.
- Write the kind of work, never the customer: "refunding a module bought twice", not their name. No ids, no e-mail addresses, no credentials.
- This is not shown to the person and it is not a summary of the conversation. One line before, one line after. Do not narrate it, do not ask permission for it, and do not let it interrupt the work.
- A single lookup needs no frame. Opening one for every question would bury the signal in noise.
@endif
